DepotDownloader
---------------
  Version:   3.4.0 (GitHub release DepotDownloader_3.4.0; official linux-x64 build)
  License:   GNU General Public License v2.0 (GPL-2.0)
  Source:    https://github.com/SteamRE/DepotDownloader/tree/DepotDownloader_3.4.0
  Release:   https://github.com/SteamRE/DepotDownloader/releases/tag/DepotDownloader_3.4.0
  In image:  /opt/depotdownloader/DepotDownloader  the unmodified release binary
             /opt/depotdownloader/LICENSE          the GPL-2.0 text, as shipped in the release zip
             /opt/depotdownloader/RELEASE.txt      asset name, download URL and the sha256 verified at build

  DepotDownloader is used exactly as SteamRE released it. The Dockerfile downloads the zip by pinned
  version and sha256 (ARG DD_VERSION, DD_SHA256_AMD64), verifies it and unpacks it; it is not built
  from source, not modified and not vendored into this repository. The image runs it as a separate
  program: at build time to fetch the game files from Steam, and at run time for UPDATE_ON_START and
  AUTO_UPDATE_INTERVAL_MINUTES, always with Steam's anonymous dedicated-server access. The GPL-2.0
  applies to DepotDownloader itself; its corresponding source is the tagged tree linked above.

Don't Starve Together dedicated server
--------------------------------------
  The game files under /app (bin64/, data/, mods/, the Steamworks redistributables steamclient.so and
  libsteamwebrtc.so) are downloaded from Steam (app 343050) with the anonymous dedicated-server
  subscription. They belong to Klei Entertainment and their respective owners and are not covered by
  this repository's license.

Debian
------
  The base image, debian:trixie-slim, carries its own licenses: https://hub.docker.com/_/debian.

Prior art
---------
  Jamesits/docker-dst-server (https://github.com/Jamesits/docker-dst-server, GPL-2.0) was the
  reference for this image's behaviour (port layout, the /data mount, the ~5 minute save on stop).
  No code or file from that repository is included here; this is an independent implementation,
  structurally modelled on stargumbo/necesse-server (MIT).
